# .gitignore — what never belongs in this repository, and why.
#
# Three rules shape this file:
#   1. A secret is never committed, not even an example with a real value in it.
#   2. Anything derived from a document is treated as private. Candidates, rendered
#      pages, reports and logs can all reveal the contents of someone's file, so the
#      run directory is ignored as a whole rather than file by file.
#   3. Anything large and not ours stays out: the unpacked LibreOffice payload, model
#      weights, virtual environments and installed packages are reproducible from
#      `requirements.txt`, `package.json` and the documented setup commands.
#
# Patterns here are deliberately broad. Where a broad pattern would swallow a file
# the project genuinely needs, the exception is written out immediately below it so
# the reason stays visible.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials and local configuration
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SENTRY_DSN, GEMMA_MODEL, SOFFICE_PATH and friends are read from the environment at
# runtime (see OBSERVABILITY.md). They are never read from a committed file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
*.crt
secrets.json
.sentryclirc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python environments, caches and tooling output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
.nox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node and the Vite frontend
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# frontend/.gitignore carries the detail; these repeat the essentials so a clone from
# the project root is clean even if that file is missing.
node_modules/
.npm/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Playwright's downloaded browser binaries and run output. The browsers live in the
# user's own cache directory; these cover the case where a run writes beside the repo.
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright/
playwright/.cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local tool payloads
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The unpacked LibreOffice is hundreds of megabytes and is not ours. It is installed
# per-machine, found on PATH, or unpacked here with the msiexec command in README.md.
.tools/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model weights
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Should any ever be placed in the tree. Models live in the runtime's own store
# (Ollama's models directory), never in this repository.
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.onnx
models/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run artefacts: anything derived from a document
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `work/` is where every CLI run, evaluation and API server writes: uploaded copies,
# patched candidates, rendered page images, pipeline.json reports and logs. Ignoring
# the directory is the same privacy rule that applies to the document itself.
work/
*.docx
*.pdf
*.log

# The one deliberate exception to `*.docx`: the hand-testing kit. Every file in
# test-documents/ is generated by make_test_documents.py from the synthetic fixture
# builders in this repository, so none of them is a real person's document, and they
# are committed because "download the test kit" must not mean "run a script first".
# The negation has to name the directory before the files, or git never descends
# into it to reconsider them.
!test-documents/
!test-documents/*.docx

# Rendered pages and screenshots. Browser evidence is written under work/ or a
# scratch directory by default; a synthetic-fixture screenshot that is genuinely worth
# keeping has to be added deliberately with `git add -f`, so a real document's page
# can never be committed by an untracked-file sweep.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.webp
*.gif
*.bmp
*.tif
*.tiff

# The README's diagrams are drawn artwork, not document evidence, so they are
# exempt from the sweep above. Nothing here is rendered from a real document.
!docs/diagrams/*.png
!docs/video/*.gif

# The exception: the interface's own artwork and anything else shipped as a static
# asset of the app. These are drawn for this project and contain no document content.
!frontend/public/**
!frontend/src/assets/**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and operating systems
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent tooling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rules files dropped in by locally installed agent plugins. They describe the
# developer's own tools, not this project, so they stay on the machine they came from.
.agents/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch space
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Somewhere to put a throwaway file without it showing up as untracked.
scratch/
tmp/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
